title: Authorizations › Worklist › Sites: what each viewer sees
route: /authorizations
intro: How the list follows the viewer and the site switch in the top bar. Every row, view count, deadline count, the average chance, the sidebar badge, the payer-signal count and the bulk review buttons are worked out from the records at the sites in view, so Site A plus Site B is Both sites. A viewer who may see one site never sees, counts, searches, signs or links to the other site's records.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: a record's site is fixed by the demo (the case ID decides, see src/data/sites.ts; a denial added from a letter carries its own site). The viewer is chosen in the Demo menu under 'Viewing as'; a fresh load starts as Jordan Perez on Both sites.
---
start s1 "Open Authorizations"
start s2 "Demo menu › 'Viewing as' › pick a viewer"
decision dV "How many sites may the viewer see?"
process v1 "Two: Jordan Perez (UR coordinator) or Alex Morgan (clinic owner)"
process v2 "One: Dr. Rivera sees Site A only, Sam Okafor sees Site B only"
screen sw "Top bar switch\n'Both sites', 'Site A', 'Site B'"
screen lk "Top bar shows a locked 'Site A only' (or 'Site B only')"
click c1 "Click 'Both sites', 'Site A' or 'Site B'"
store sc "The sites in view are kept for the session\nA new viewer starts on their only site, or on Both sites"

process p1 "The list keeps only the rows at the sites in view\nA denial follows its own site; any other record follows its case"
screen h1 "Title 'Authorizations' with a small 'Site A' tag when one site is in view"
screen ch "View chips\nSite A: All 55, Needs attention 19, In progress 14, With the payer 20, Approved 17, Denied 4, Reviews this week 26\nSite B: All 40, 11, 5, 16, 15, 4, 21"
doc eq "Both sites = Site A + Site B for every count\n95 = 55 + 40, 30 = 19 + 11, 47 = 26 + 21\nAn average does not add: it is worked out again"
process sb "Sidebar badge on 'Authorizations': 19 = Site A 11 + Site B 8"
process sg "Payer signal: Site A 'Review it' (one), Site B 'Review the three'"
process fl "Search, every filter and ?quick= reach only rows in view\nA ?quick= for the other site's request is dropped; its ?review= opens nothing"
process bu "'Draft all due reviews' and 'Sign all clean drafts' act only on reviews at the sites in view"
click l1 "Open a case at the other site by its address\n/authorizations/case/ID"
goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › Case page › A case at another site"
goto g2 "Continues in: Authorizations › Reviews this week › Draft all due reviews and sign all clean drafts"
goto g3 "Continues in: Authorizations › Worklist › Cardinal payer signal"

s1 --> dV
s2 --> sc
dV -->|Two| v1 --> sw --> c1 --> sc
dV -->|One| v2 --> lk
sc --> p1
lk --> p1
p1 --> h1
p1 --> ch
p1 --> sb
p1 --> sg
p1 --> fl
p1 --> bu
ch -.-> eq
sb -.-> eq
sg -.-> g3
bu -.-> g2
fl --> l1 --> g1
